---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = "June 2025";
const siteName    = "Tools & Games Hub";
const siteUrl     = "https://toolsandgameshub.com"; // ← update before launch
const contactEmail = "privacy@toolsandgameshub.com"; // ← update before launch
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">

    <!-- Page header -->
    <div class="mb-8">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 tracking-tight mb-1">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Policy card -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl shadow-sm px-8 py-10 flex flex-col gap-8 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">

      <!-- 1. Introduction -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p>
          {siteName} ("<strong>we</strong>", "<strong>our</strong>", or "<strong>us</strong>") operates the website
          located at <a href={siteUrl} class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline">{siteUrl}</a> (the "Service").
          This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you
          visit our website. Please read this policy carefully. If you disagree with its terms, please
          discontinue use of the Service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Information we collect -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">We may collect the following categories of information:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside flex flex-col gap-2 pl-2">
          <li><strong>Log Data:</strong> Your browser type, IP address, pages visited, time and date of your visit, and other diagnostic data automatically transmitted by your browser.</li>
          <li><strong>Usage Data:</strong> Information about how you interact with our tools and games (e.g., feature usage, session duration), collected in aggregate and non-identifiable form.</li>
          <li><strong>Cookies and Tracking Technologies:</strong> First-party and third-party cookies, web beacons, pixels, and similar tracking technologies as described in Section 5 below.</li>
          <li><strong>Voluntarily Submitted Data:</strong> Any information you provide through our Contact form, including your email address and message content.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. How we use your information -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">We use collected information to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside flex flex-col gap-2 pl-2">
          <li>Operate, maintain, and improve the Service.</li>
          <li>Respond to enquiries submitted via the Contact form.</li>
          <li>Monitor and analyse usage trends and diagnostic data to enhance user experience.</li>
          <li>Detect, prevent, and address technical issues, fraud, or illegal activity.</li>
          <li>Serve relevant advertisements through our third-party advertising partners (see Section 5).</li>
          <li>Comply with applicable legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. Legal basis (GDPR) -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">4. Legal Basis for Processing (GDPR)</h2>
        <p>
          For users located in the European Economic Area (EEA), our legal basis for collecting and using personal
          information is: (a) your <strong>consent</strong> where we have requested it; (b) the performance of a
          contract where processing is necessary to provide the Service; (c) our <strong>legitimate interests</strong>
          in operating and improving the Service, provided these are not overridden by your data-protection rights;
          and (d) compliance with our <strong>legal obligations</strong>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Cookies & Third-Party Advertising (AdSense) -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">5. Cookies &amp; Third-Party Advertising</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          We use cookies — small text files stored on your device — to enhance functionality and to serve
          personalised advertisements. Our advertising partner is <strong>Google AdSense</strong>, operated by
          Google LLC ("Google").
        </p>
        <p class="mb-3">
          <strong>How Google AdSense uses cookies:</strong> Google AdSense uses cookies such as the
          <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono">DSID</code>,
          <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono">FLC</code>,
          <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono">AID</code>,
          <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono">TAID</code>, and
          <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono">exchange_uid</code> cookies to serve
          ads based on your prior visits to this website or other websites on the internet. These cookies enable
          Google and its partners to serve ads based on your visit to our site and/or other sites on the internet.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-3">
          <strong>DoubleClick DART Cookie:</strong> Google, as a third-party vendor, uses the DART cookie to
          serve ads to visitors based on their visit to {siteName} and other sites on the internet. Users may opt
          out of the use of the DART cookie by visiting the
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline">Google ad and content network privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-3">
          <strong>Your choices:</strong> You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
          <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline">aboutads.info</a>
          or the <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline">NAI opt-out page</a>.
          EU/EEA users may additionally manage consent through our cookie consent banner.
          You can also disable cookies entirely through your browser settings; note that doing so may affect site functionality.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google's use of advertising cookies is governed by
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
          We have no control over, and assume no responsibility for, the content or privacy practices of
          third-party sites or services linked from advertisements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. Data sharing -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">6. Data Sharing &amp; Disclosure</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">We do not sell, trade, or rent your personal information. We may share data with:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside flex flex-col gap-2 pl-2">
          <li><strong>Service Providers:</strong> Trusted third parties who assist us in operating the website (e.g., hosting providers, analytics platforms), bound by confidentiality obligations.</li>
          <li><strong>Advertising Partners:</strong> Google AdSense, as described in Section 5.</li>
          <li><strong>Legal Requirements:</strong> Authorities when required by law, court order, or to protect our rights and the safety of others.</li>
          <li><strong>Business Transfers:</strong> A successor entity in the event of a merger, acquisition, or asset sale, subject to standard confidentiality protections.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 7. Data retention -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">7. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain personal data only as long as necessary for the purposes outlined in this policy, or as
          required by law. Contact form submissions are retained for up to 24 months for correspondence purposes
          and then securely deleted. Anonymised aggregate analytics data may be retained indefinitely.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 8. Children's privacy -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">8. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Our Service is not directed to children under the age of 13 (or 16 in the EEA). We do not knowingly
          collect personally identifiable information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with
          personal data, please contact us immediately and we will take steps to delete such information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 9. Security -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">9. Security</h2>
        <p>
          We implement commercially reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your information.
          However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure. We cannot
          guarantee absolute security and encourage you to use the Service with appropriate discretion.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 10. Your rights -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">10. Your Rights</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside flex flex-col gap-2 pl-2">
          <li>Access the personal data we hold about you.</li>
          <li>Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
          <li>Request deletion of your personal data ("right to be forgotten").</li>
          <li>Object to or restrict certain processing activities.</li>
          <li>Request data portability in a machine-readable format.</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent at any time (where processing is based on consent).</li>
          <li>Lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline">{contactEmail}</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- 11. Changes to this policy -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">11. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. Any changes will be posted on this page with a revised
          "Last updated" date. Continued use of the Service after any changes constitutes your acceptance of
          the updated policy. We encourage you to review this page regularly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 12. Contact -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">12. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:<br />
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline">{contactEmail}</a>
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SEO / crawler context -->
  <div slot="description">
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy governs the collection and use of data on {siteName}, including the use of
      Google AdSense advertising cookies, third-party tracking technologies, and user-submitted contact information.
      We are committed to transparency and full compliance with applicable data-protection regulations including
      GDPR and CCPA.
    </p>
  </div>

</Layout>
